WHATNOW

What tam-knox is doing now and what comes next. Read this first;
revise it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W11

STATE

  Version 1.1.2 on branch dev (follows tam-idol 1.3.0; ROADMAP.md updated
  in W11). Phases P1 (0.1.0-0.1.2), P2 (0.2.0), and
  P3 (0.3.0-1.0.6), 1.0.7-1.1.1 (libtam 0.10.0-0.14.1), and 1.1.2
  (scrollable word-wrapped guidance modal) are complete and pass make
  test, make sanitize, and idol-check.

  Features working in 1.0.5:
  - Multi-repository Source Control sidebar (repository discovery,
    branch name, dirty/clean state, changed files list, ahead/behind
    count, path-scoped staging and committing, single-repo remote fetch
    via f, single-repo remote sync via s / Alt+S with protected-branch
    confirmation, and non-destructive multi-repo batch fetch via
    Alt+A / F).
  - Interactive Branch Checkout and Creation modal (Alt+K or c) and
    Stash Management modal (Alt+Z or z).
  - Side-by-Side Split Diff mode (d, D, Alt+D, or R in Diff Viewer).
  - Git Graph commit history using the Vertex/Branch/determinePath lane
    layout algorithm from mhutchie.git-graph, with inline ref badges and
    a split Commit Details and Changed Files diff inspector.
  - Folder Explorer tree with live Git status badges, live
    case-insensitive substring filtering (/ or Ctrl+F, Esc to clear),
    Return/Right on a repo to open and expand it in Explorer, Right/Left
    to expand/collapse folders and move focus between Explorer and File
    Viewer, and Backspace to return to Source Control.
  - Optional user keymap.ini configuration via libtam tam_ini
    (~/.config/tamlinux/tam-knox/keymap.ini or TAM_KNOX_KEYMAP).
  - File and Diff Viewer with C11 syntax coloring and tam-view Markdown,
    HTML, and Mermaid rendering, tabs (direct 1-9 and 0 focus/selection
    with on-demand top-bar title shrinking), split panes, command
    palette, and keybinding guidance (g / Ctrl+G).

